            <ArticleTitle>Placenta percreta causing acute abdomen in the second trimester of pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>244-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of acute abdomen due to haemoperitoneum caused by placenta percreta in the second trimester are presented. Both had a history of previous lower segment caesarean section, a factor well-known to predispose the condition. However, the rarity of the condition, presenting in mid pregnancy makes diagnosis and management difficult. Optimum ways of management are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
